"""Molly O'Shea, part A: biography (Origins, Red Dead Redemption 2 chapters 1 to 6).

Sources (Red Dead Wiki EN, Oct 2026, saved in scratchpad cov/molly/ and cov/molly/m/): character page "Molly O'Shea"
(Background, Events of Red Dead Redemption 2, Mission Appearances, Trivia); FR page "Molly O'Shea" (fr.txt, used only
as a check: it wrongly puts her death in chapter 6 and her disappearance at Shady Belle); transcripts "/dialogues" of
"Outlaws from the West" (Susan's room allocation), "Polite Society, Valentine Style" (Tilly and Karen), "Who is Not
Without Sin" (her line), "Blessed are the Peacemakers" (opening: Arthur asks her where Dutch is), "The Battle of Shady
Belle" (she asks Dutch for a word on arrival), "Red Dead Redemption" (Milton at Van Horn; Arthur's lines in the
endings); mission pages "Eastward Bound", "A Quiet Time", "An Honest Mistake" (infobox: giver Molly O'Shea/Uncle),
"Blood Feuds, Ancient and Modern", "The Battle of Shady Belle", "Horsemen, Apocalypses" (failure if any gang member is
killed), "Banking, The Old American Art" (trivia: she is not at the heist), "That's Murfree Country" (Story, Deaths,
infobox chapter 5); "Camp Events" (Lakay: Arthur can ask where Molly is, missing since the heist; Beaver Hollow:
Karen and Susan). No transcript exists on the wiki for "An Honest Mistake", "A Quiet Time", "Blood Feuds",
"Horsemen, Apocalypses" or "That's Murfree Country" (checked via the API, 20 Oct 2026): those scenes are told from the
mission pages and the character page, without quotation marks.
Cross-checked against the fact-checked parts dutch_A/B/C, arthur_B/C/D, susan_A, uncle_A, hosea_B, micah_A, orville_A,
kieran_A, karen_A, tilly_A, simon_A, bill_A: Susan shoots her in the stomach with a pump-action shotgun at the end of
chapter 5, in "That's Murfree Country", at Beaver Hollow (fc 20 Oct: the mission page says only "a shotgun", as in the Susan fiche, so the type is left out here); Uncle "found her in Saint Denis" is attributed to the wiki
(uncle_A); Milton's three days are conditional on Dutch surrendering (uncle rules); Shady Belle is cleared of Lemoyne
Raiders (susan report); Milton tells Arthur at Van Horn that she never talked; the low-honor "Not Molly... not Miss
Grimshaw..." line belongs to the money ending only (susan report) and is said AFTER Micah stabs Arthur and Dutch
arrives and stops him (transcript l.686-710).
Fact-check fixes (20 Oct 2026): the guide says she CLAIMS a well-to-do family (attributed, Personality owns it);
Lakay order (Fleeting Joy attack, then Arthur asks); Guarma-period sentence removed (unsupported); quarrels named only
with Karen; chapter 4 sentence split; dangling Colter cross-reference removed; death-scene details added from the
character page, attributed (no transcript).

Ownership: official descriptions (Rockstar, Sept. 2018; official guide wording), personality, names ("Miss O'Shea",
"Your Majesty"), appearance, the poem, the mirror, and camp scenes (Dutch in his tent at Colter and his flirting,
"Dutch is all the company I need", the arguments with Dutch, Abigail's advice, the fights with Karen, Tilly and the
chores, Sean, the party dances, the party after Jack's return, the dock scenes, her talk with Arthur after Kieran's
death, Karen calling Susan a murderer, Mary-Beth and Tilly afterwards) go to part B; this part points to them in one
clause at most. Lines quoted in part C are paraphrased here without quotation marks.

Excluded: the "foreshadowing" of her death in Tilly's dominoes activity and in the broken mirror (interpretation); the
wiki trivia reading her An Honest Mistake lines as a reference to a Pinkerton interrogation (speculation); the exact
wording of her lines in "An Honest Mistake" and "That's Murfree Country" (no transcript: paraphrased and attributed);
Wikipedia's "gunshot to the chest" (the mission page, the character page and arthur_C say stomach); Fleeting Joy's
"presumably intentional" note on her absence (speculation); "Supposedly" wealthy (kept as the guide's statement,
attributed); the FR wiki's claim that she told the Pinkertons where the camp was (her claim concerned the bank job);
the cut grave and the cut "Gilded Cage" outfit (cut content, part D); "most of the gang believed she got what she
deserved" and "possibly Arthur" (interpretation).
"""


def two(en, fr): return {"en": en, "fr": fr}


BLOCKS = [
    # ================================================================ Origins
    {"h3": two("Origins", "Origines"), "year": ""},
    {"p": two("The games give no date of birth for Molly. She is Irish and comes from Dublin. Her family background is known only from what she claims, as reported by an official guide (see Personality). When and how she joined the gang is not told; by 1899 she is the companion of [[dutch-van-der-linde|Dutch van der Linde]] and shares his tent.",
              "Les jeux ne donnent aucune date de naissance pour Molly. Elle est irlandaise, originaire de Dublin. De sa famille, on ne sait que ce qu'elle en dit elle-même, selon un guide officiel (voir Personnalité). On ignore quand et comment elle a rejoint la bande ; en 1899, elle est la compagne de [[dutch-van-der-linde|Dutch van der Linde]] et partage sa tente.")},

    # ================================================================ RDR2 1899
    {"h3": two("Red Dead Redemption 2 (1899)", "Red Dead Redemption 2 (1899)"), "year": "1899"},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 1: Colter", "Chapitre 1 : Colter"), "chapter": 1},
    {"p": two("After the failed ferry robbery in Blackwater, the gang takes shelter in Colter, an abandoned mining town in the snow. In \"Outlaws from the West\", Dutch comes back from the Adler homestead with [[sadie-adler|Sadie Adler]] and says he needs rest. [[susan-grimshaw|Susan Grimshaw]] points him to his cabin and says that Molly will show him the way. Molly stays with Dutch for the rest of the chapter. The Red Dead Wiki also lists her in \"Eastward Bound\", the move down from the mountains to Horseshoe Overlook, above Valentine; the mission page does not name her.",
              "Après l'échec du braquage du ferry à Blackwater, la bande se réfugie à Colter, une ville minière abandonnée sous la neige. Dans \"Outlaws from the West\", Dutch revient de la ferme des Adler avec [[sadie-adler|Sadie Adler]] et dit avoir besoin de repos. [[susan-grimshaw|Susan Grimshaw]] lui désigne sa cabane et annonce que Molly va l'y conduire. Molly reste auprès de Dutch jusqu'à la fin du chapitre. Le Red Dead Wiki la cite aussi dans \"Eastward Bound\", la descente des montagnes vers Horseshoe Overlook, au-dessus de Valentine ; la page de la mission ne la nomme pas.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 2: Horseshoe Overlook", "Chapitre 2 : Horseshoe Overlook"), "chapter": 2},
    {"p": two("In \"Polite Society, Valentine Style\", [[arthur-morgan|Arthur Morgan]] and [[uncle|Uncle]] take [[karen-jones|Karen Jones]], [[tilly-jackson|Tilly Jackson]] and [[mary-beth-gaskill|Mary-Beth Gaskill]] into Valentine. On the way, Tilly wonders whether they should have asked Molly along, and Karen mocks her airs (see Quotes). According to the character page of the Red Dead Wiki, Molly is in camp, in \"A Quiet Time\", when [[lenny-summers|Lenny Summers]] tells Dutch and Arthur that [[micah-bell|Micah Bell]] has been arrested in Strawberry.",
              "Dans \"Polite Society, Valentine Style\", [[arthur-morgan|Arthur Morgan]] et [[uncle|Uncle]] emmènent [[karen-jones|Karen Jones]], [[tilly-jackson|Tilly Jackson]] et [[mary-beth-gaskill|Mary-Beth Gaskill]] à Valentine. En chemin, Tilly se demande s'il aurait fallu proposer à Molly de venir, et Karen raille ses grands airs (voir Citations). D'après la page du personnage sur le Red Dead Wiki, Molly est au camp, dans \"A Quiet Time\", quand [[lenny-summers|Lenny Summers]] annonce à Dutch et à Arthur que [[micah-bell|Micah Bell]] a été arrêté à Strawberry.")},
    {"p": two("In \"Who is Not Without Sin\", Arthur brings [[orville-swanson|Reverend Swanson]] back from Flatneck Station, unconscious and drunk, and carries him through the camp to his tent. Molly sees them arrive and remarks that she had been wondering when the reverend would turn up. Her camp scenes of the chapter, including her dance with Dutch at the party for [[sean-macguire|Sean MacGuire]]'s return, are covered under Relationships. At the end of the chapter, the gang leaves Horseshoe Overlook for Clemens Point, on Flat Iron Lake in Lemoyne.",
              "Dans \"Who is Not Without Sin\", Arthur ramène de Flatneck Station le [[orville-swanson|révérend Swanson]], ivre mort, et le porte à travers le camp jusqu'à sa tente. Molly les voit arriver et fait remarquer qu'elle se demandait quand le révérend finirait par se montrer. Ses scènes de camp du chapitre, dont sa danse avec Dutch pendant la fête donnée pour le retour de [[sean-macguire|Sean MacGuire]], sont racontées dans les relations. À la fin du chapitre, la bande quitte Horseshoe Overlook pour Clemens Point, au bord du lac Flat Iron, en Lemoyne.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 3: Clemens Point", "Chapitre 3 : Clemens Point"), "chapter": 3},
    {"p": two("At Clemens Point, Molly and Dutch argue more and more often (see Relationships). \"An Honest Mistake\", which the Red Dead Wiki credits to Molly and Uncle as mission givers, opens with Molly calling Arthur over to talk about Dutch. According to the character page, she asks Arthur how Dutch seems to him, says that she really loves him and starts to recall his saying that loyalty is everything. Uncle interrupts with a tip about a supply wagon he believes is unguarded, and Arthur leaves with him, [[charles-smith|Charles Smith]] and [[bill-williamson|Bill Williamson]].",
              "À Clemens Point, Molly et Dutch se disputent de plus en plus souvent (voir Relations). \"An Honest Mistake\", dont le Red Dead Wiki attribue la mission à Molly et à Uncle, s'ouvre sur Molly qui appelle Arthur pour lui parler de Dutch. D'après la page du personnage, elle lui demande comment il trouve Dutch, assure qu'elle l'aime vraiment et commence à rappeler sa maxime selon laquelle la loyauté passe avant tout. Uncle les interrompt avec un tuyau sur un chariot de ravitaillement qu'il croit sans escorte, et Arthur part avec lui, [[charles-smith|Charles Smith]] et [[bill-williamson|Bill Williamson]].")},
    {"p": two("\"Blessed are the Peacemakers\" opens at Clemens Point as Arthur greets Micah. Arthur asks Molly where Dutch is. She waves him off and keeps walking. The Red Dead Wiki also lists her in \"Blood Feuds, Ancient and Modern\", in which the men ride to Braithwaite Manor to find [[jack-marston|Jack Marston]]; she is not among the riders, and the mission page does not name her. The next morning, in \"The Battle of Shady Belle\", the Pinkerton agents [[andrew-milton|Andrew Milton]] and [[edgar-ross|Edgar Ross]] come to Clemens Point. Milton offers the others three days to disappear if Dutch gives himself up. The gang refuses and leaves for Shady Belle, an abandoned plantation house near Saint Denis that Arthur and [[john-marston|John Marston]] clear of Lemoyne Raiders.",
              "\"Blessed are the Peacemakers\" s'ouvre à Clemens Point alors qu'Arthur salue Micah. Arthur demande à Molly où est Dutch. Elle l'écarte d'un geste et continue son chemin. Le Red Dead Wiki la cite aussi dans \"Blood Feuds, Ancient and Modern\", où les hommes chevauchent jusqu'au manoir Braithwaite pour retrouver [[jack-marston|Jack Marston]] ; elle ne fait pas partie des cavaliers, et la page de la mission ne la nomme pas. Le lendemain matin, dans \"The Battle of Shady Belle\", les agents de la Pinkerton [[andrew-milton|Andrew Milton]] et [[edgar-ross|Edgar Ross]] se présentent à Clemens Point. Milton propose aux autres trois jours pour disparaître si Dutch se rend. La bande refuse et part pour Shady Belle, une demeure de plantation abandonnée près de Saint-Denis qu'Arthur et [[john-marston|John Marston]] vident des Lemoyne Raiders.")},
    {"p": two("When the caravan reaches Shady Belle, Dutch asks Susan and [[simon-pearson|Simon Pearson]] to set up the camp and tells Arthur to ride with him. Molly calls out to Dutch and asks him for a word. Dutch tells her not now and rides off with Arthur. On the road to Saint Denis, he complains to Arthur that she wants to talk when he has so much going on, and says he has far more important things to worry about than her.",
              "Quand le convoi arrive à Shady Belle, Dutch charge Susan et [[simon-pearson|Simon Pearson]] d'installer le camp et demande à Arthur de l'accompagner. Molly interpelle Dutch et lui demande de lui parler. Dutch répond que ce n'est pas le moment et part avec Arthur. Sur la route de Saint-Denis, il se plaint à Arthur qu'elle veuille discuter alors qu'il a tant à faire, et déclare qu'il a bien plus important à penser qu'elle.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 4: Saint Denis", "Chapitre 4 : Saint-Denis"), "chapter": 4},
    {"p": two("At Shady Belle, Molly keeps away from Dutch and from most of the camp; her camp scenes of the chapter, among them the party after Jack's return from [[angelo-bronte|Angelo Bronte]]'s mansion and Karen's attempt to talk to her on the dock, are covered under Relationships. In \"Horsemen, Apocalypses\", the O'Driscolls send [[kieran-duffy|Kieran Duffy]]'s mutilated body into the camp on a horse and attack Shady Belle. Molly takes no part in the fighting. As with the other members who stay out of the fight, the mission fails if she is killed. After the battle, she talks to Arthur about Kieran's and Sean's deaths (see Relationships).",
              "À Shady Belle, Molly se tient à l'écart de Dutch et de la plus grande partie du camp ; ses scènes de camp du chapitre, dont la fête qui suit le retour de Jack, tiré de la demeure d'[[angelo-bronte|Angelo Bronte]], et la tentative de Karen pour lui parler sur le ponton, sont racontées dans les relations. Dans \"Horsemen, Apocalypses\", les O'Driscoll renvoient à cheval dans le camp le corps mutilé de [[kieran-duffy|Kieran Duffy]], puis attaquent Shady Belle. Molly ne prend pas part au combat. Comme pour les autres membres qui restent à l'écart du combat, sa mort fait échouer la mission. Après la bataille, elle parle à Arthur de la mort de Kieran et de celle de Sean (voir Relations).")},
    {"p": two("Molly is one of the members who take no part in \"Banking, The Old American Art\", the robbery of the Saint Denis bank. The job fails. [[hosea-matthews|Hosea Matthews]] and Lenny are killed. John is arrested. Dutch, Arthur, Micah, Bill and [[javier-escuella|Javier Escuella]] escape on a ship and end up on the island of Guarma. Molly's camp scenes stop for good after the robbery.",
              "Molly fait partie des membres qui ne participent pas à \"Banking, The Old American Art\", le braquage de la banque de Saint-Denis. Le coup échoue. [[hosea-matthews|Hosea Matthews]] et Lenny sont tués. John est arrêté. Dutch, Arthur, Micah, Bill et [[javier-escuella|Javier Escuella]] s'enfuient sur un navire et échouent sur l'île de Guarma. Les scènes de camp de Molly disparaissent définitivement après le braquage.")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 5: Guarma", "Chapitre 5 : Guarma"), "chapter": 5},
    {"p": two("The survivors of Guarma rejoin the gang at Lakay, in the bayou, and the Pinkertons attack the camp in \"Fleeting Joy\". Afterwards, Arthur can ask the others where Molly is; she has been missing since the bank job. According to the character page of the Red Dead Wiki, several members, among them Susan, worry about her absence. Dutch decides that the gang must move north. In \"That's Murfree Country\", Arthur and Charles clear a cave at Beaver Hollow, in Roanoke Ridge, of the Murfree Brood, and the gang settles there.",
              "Les rescapés de Guarma retrouvent la bande à Lakay, dans le bayou, et les Pinkerton attaquent le camp dans \"Fleeting Joy\". Ensuite, Arthur peut demander aux autres où est passée Molly ; elle a disparu depuis le braquage. D'après la page du personnage sur le Red Dead Wiki, plusieurs membres, dont Susan, s'inquiètent de son absence. Dutch décide que la bande doit remonter vers le nord. Dans \"That's Murfree Country\", Arthur et Charles débarrassent une grotte de Beaver Hollow, dans Roanoke Ridge, de la Murfree Brood, et la bande s'y installe.")},
    {"p": two("While the new camp is being set up, Uncle arrives with Molly, who is drunk; according to the Red Dead Wiki, he says he found her in Saint Denis. In front of the gang, she berates Dutch for ignoring her. According to the character page, she says she loved him and mockingly calls him the Lord God almighty; Dutch points out that she is drunk and tells her to calm down. She then claims that she told the Pinkertons about the Saint Denis bank job, hoping, according to the same page, that Milton and Ross would kill Dutch. Dutch draws his revolver to kill her. Arthur tries to stop him; the character page has him call Molly a fool who is not worth Dutch's time. Before Dutch can fire, Susan shoots Molly in the stomach with a shotgun and kills her.",
              "Pendant l'installation du nouveau camp, Uncle arrive avec Molly, ivre ; d'après le Red Dead Wiki, il dit l'avoir trouvée à Saint-Denis. Devant toute la bande, elle reproche à Dutch de l'ignorer. D'après la page du personnage, elle lui crie qu'elle l'aimait et le traite, par dérision, de Seigneur Dieu tout-puissant ; Dutch lui fait remarquer qu'elle est ivre et lui demande de se calmer. Elle affirme ensuite avoir renseigné les Pinkerton sur le braquage de la banque de Saint-Denis, dans l'espoir, toujours selon cette page, que Milton et Ross tuent Dutch. Dutch sort son revolver pour l'abattre. Arthur tente de l'en empêcher ; sur la page du personnage, il dit que Molly n'est qu'une idiote qui ne mérite pas que Dutch perde son temps. Avant que Dutch ne tire, Susan lui tire dessus au fusil, en plein ventre, et la tue.")},
    {"p": two("Susan tells Arthur that Molly knew the rules. She orders Bill and Pearson to burn the body. The killing closes the fifth chapter, and completing that chapter unlocks the trophy titled No Traitors. Karen turns on Susan right after the shooting (see Relationships).",
              "Susan rappelle à Arthur que Molly connaissait les règles. Elle ordonne à Bill et à Pearson de brûler le corps. Cette exécution clôt le cinquième chapitre, dont l'achèvement débloque le trophée No Traitors. Karen s'en prend à Susan juste après le coup de feu (voir Relations).")},

    {"h4": two("Chapter 6: Beaver Hollow", "Chapitre 6 : Beaver Hollow"), "chapter": 6},
    {"p": two("In \"Red Dead Redemption\", the last mission of the chapter, Arthur and Sadie go to Van Horn to free [[abigail-marston|Abigail Marston]], held by Milton. Milton holds Arthur at gunpoint and says that not every member of the gang had his scruples, then names Micah. Arthur asks whether he means Molly. Milton answers that the Pinkertons questioned Molly a couple of times, that she never said a word and that they had to let her go. Micah, he says, was picked up when the gang came back from the Caribbean and has worked for them ever since. Abigail then shoots Milton.",
              "Dans \"Red Dead Redemption\", dernière mission du chapitre, Arthur et Sadie se rendent à Van Horn pour libérer [[abigail-marston|Abigail Marston]], aux mains de Milton. Milton tient Arthur en joue et lui dit que tous les membres de la bande n'avaient pas ses scrupules, puis nomme Micah. Arthur demande s'il parle de Molly. Milton répond que les Pinkerton ont interrogé Molly à deux ou trois reprises, qu'elle n'a jamais dit un mot et qu'ils ont dû la relâcher. Micah, en revanche, a été cueilli au retour des Caraïbes et travaille pour eux depuis. Abigail abat ensuite Milton.")},
    {"p": two("Back at Beaver Hollow, Arthur tells the gang that Micah is the informant. In the two endings in which Arthur goes back for the money, he tells Dutch, during his confrontation with Micah, that the traitor is Micah and not Molly. With low honor, he says it after Micah has stabbed him in the chest and Dutch has arrived and stopped Micah, and he clears Susan and Colm in the same breath.",
              "De retour à Beaver Hollow, Arthur annonce à la bande que l'informateur est Micah. Dans les deux fins où Arthur retourne chercher l'argent, il affirme à Dutch, au cours de son affrontement avec Micah, que le traître est Micah et non Molly. Avec un honneur bas, il le dit après que Micah l'a poignardé à la poitrine et que Dutch, arrivé sur les lieux, a retenu Micah ; dans la même phrase, il disculpe aussi Susan et Colm.")},
]
